  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to UN Reforms in Kenya - Support to UN Reforms in Kenya via UNDP</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to UN Reforms in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta f&#xf6;rslag har fokus p&#xe5; kritiska funktioner, aktiviteter och kostnader f&#xf6;r FN:s representanter i Kenya (Resident Coordinators) och syftar till att kontorets (Resident Coordinator Office, RCO) ompositioneringsarbete inte tappar fart eller att det uppst&#xe5;r kapacitetsbrist n&#xe4;r nya modeller f&#xf6;r global finansiering av RC/RCO-funktionen med f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkta befogenheter stegvis inr&#xe4;ttas i fler &#xe4;n 150 l&#xe4;nder runtom i v&#xe4;rlden. F&#xf6;rslaget omfattar b&#xe5;de den RC/RCO-funktion som &#xe4;r utan finansiering fr&#xe5;n januari 2019 och funktioner som kan riskera att f&#xf6;rsvagas under transitionsfasen. F&#xf6;reslaget bidrar till att bibeh&#xe5;lla takten p&#xe5; genomf&#xf6;randet av de investeringar SE gjort i FN de senaste &#xe5;ren.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal targets critical functions, activities and costs of the UN Resident Coordinators, safeguarding that momentum in RCO&#x2019;s repositioning work in Kenya is not lost or severe capacity gaps created, during a period when new modalities for global financing of the empowered RC/RCO function are gradually put in place in more than 150 countries around the world.  The proposal covers both aspects of the RC/RCO function in Kenya that are without funding from January 2019 and functions that could be undermined duringthe trasition phase.  This will help  maintain the momentum of the investments SE has made with the UN in the last few years.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal targets critical functions, activities and costs of the UN Resident Coordinators, safeguarding that momentum in RCOs repositioning work in Kenya is not lost or severe capacity gaps created, during a period when new modalities for global financing of the empowered RC/RCO function are gradually put in place</narrative>
  </description>
